.92</tspan> Oct 30 low</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"362.1\" y2=\"362.1\" stroke=\"#6B6152\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"366.1\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#6B6152\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$270.00</tspan> 52-wk low</text><circle cx=\"515.1\" cy=\"297.2\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#C9A84C\" stroke=\"#20242C\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></svg></figure>\n<p>These lines are mine, not yours: the Oct 30 low, the 52-week low, the 20-day and 200-day averages, and my 38.2% retracement of the drop from the May 18 high ($408.10) to the Oct 30 low ($276.92).</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Trend:</strong> down. Price $293.45 is under the 20-day ($308.18), the 50-day ($329.88) and the 200-day ($338.59), and the 50-day is under the 200-day.</li><li><strong>Momentum:</strong> RSI 38.0, weak but turning up from the low. The stock is 28% under its 52-week high.</li><li><strong>Ceiling:</strong> the 20-day at $308.18 first, then my 38.2% line at $327.03, which sits next to the 50-day. The day after earnings it dropped from $324.89 to $283.82, so that gap is overhead supply.</li><li><strong>Floor:</strong> $276.92 (Oct 30 low), then the 52-week low at $270.00.</li><li><strong>Your tested edge:</strong> does not apply. RSI is under 40, but this is not an uptrend: price and the 50-day are both below the 200-day.</li><li><strong>Scorecard:</strong> no open or watching play.</li><li><strong>Verdict:</strong> the chart supports the downside. It disagrees with management's picture of record demand; the market is pricing the bill, not the backlog. A close above $308.18 would be the first sign of repair and a close above $327.03 would flip the lean; a close below $276.92 confirms the down-move toward $270.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>The next report (date not found, likely late January to early February): the 2027 capital spending figure and how it will be paid for.</li><li>Any new share or bond sale before then, and the terms.</li><li>The Fed on Dec 9 and the 10-year yield: both set the cost of the debt.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Solid: results, capital spending, debt and equity figures (company release, company transcript, 10-Q). Thin: any 2027 figure; Cloud growth without chip sales; the August bond detail comes from a third-party rewrite of a Bloomberg report. Governance facts come from the 2026 proxy and press reports opened Nov 12.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001652044/000165204426000084/goog-20260930.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10-Q</a> · <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001652044/000165204426000080/googexhibit991q32026.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">earnings release</a> · <a href=\"https://s206.q4cdn.com/479360582/files/doc_events/2026/Oct/28/2026_Q3_Earnings_Transcript.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">company transcript</a> · <a href=\"https://s206.q4cdn.com/479360582/files/doc_downloads/2026/GOOG_PXY_2026_WO27_WKV_WR-IR.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2026 proxy</a> · <a href=\"https://www.clearygottlieb.com/news-and-insights/news-listing/alphabet-in-80-billion-equity-offerings-jun-2026\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cleary Gottlieb, June equity offerings</a> · <a href=\"https://www.ifre.com/equities/2437856/alphabet-storms-markets-with-historic-us90bn-equity-raise\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IFR</a> · <a href=\"https://www.bnnbloomberg.ca/investing/2026/09/22/corporate-bond-buyers-get-picky-with-flood-of-ai-debt/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BNN Bloomberg, Sept 22</a> · <a href=\"https://www.fi-desk.com/ratings-analysis-hyperscaler-spending-rings-credit-alarm-bells/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The DESK, ratings</a> · <a href=\"https://financebuzz.com/news/moodys-alphabet-ai-spending-credit-quality\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FinanceBuzz</a> · <a href=\"https://www.businesstoday.in/technology/news